0328 only adds three nullable attestation columns (legacy_reconciled_at/by/reason) plus a shape CHECK to performance_obligations; it writes no rows, backfills nothing, and offers no operator decision. The rebuild refusal and the reconcile path that consume these columns ship in application code, not in the migration. The CHECK arrives NOT VALID with a separate guarded VALIDATE step (staged build: every pre-existing row trivially holds all three NULLs, since the columns are added by this same migration), so the upgrade takes no write-blocking scan and no preflight gate is needed.
